 - `index.html` at project root, copied from the template with sample items removed and `js/app.js` wired in.
 
 **Assets:** `assets/app-spec.md` (TodoMVC spec), `assets/app-template.index.html` (base markup). These are human-owned product material under Captain custody.
+
+## Voyage 2: Browser-acceptance defect fix
+
+**Defect 1 -- DOM Identity:** The `render()` function does `todoList.innerHTML = ''` and recreates every `<li>` from scratch on every state change. A real browser (Cypress) holds a reference to a node, clicks the checkbox, and the node is destroyed mid-chain. The harness re-queries, so it never notices. Fix: mutate existing nodes in place (toggle classes, update checked state) instead of rebuilding the list.
+
+**Defect 2 -- Missing CSS:** `index.html` links only `css/app.css` (empty directory). The TodoMVC editing visibility rules live in `node_modules/todomvc-app-css/index.css` (`.todo-list li.editing .view { display: none; }`) and are never loaded. Fix: add `<link rel="stylesheet" href="node_modules/todomvc-app-css/index.css">` to `index.html`.
+
+**New specs added:**
+- `features/dom-stability.feature` (2 scenarios) -- pins DOM node identity across toggle interactions.
+- `features/edit-todo.feature` scenario "Editing mode hides the toggle and view controls" -- pins the CSS visibility requirement.
+- `features/step_definitions/app.js` -- new step definitions for identity checking and visibility assertion.
+
+**Planted red:** All 3 new scenarios fail against current code, confirming the defects are real. The 37 pre-existing scenarios remain green.
