@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+Feature: DOM node stability during state changes
+  As a user
+  I want my todo list to remain stable when I interact with it
+  So that the interface stays responsive and predictable
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo preserves existing todo nodes in the DOM
+    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    And a todo "Walk the dog" exists
+    And the todo nodes are saved for identity check
+    When the user toggles the checkbox on todo "Buy milk"
+    Then todo "Buy milk" has the completed class
+    And todo "Walk the dog" does not have the completed class
+    And all todo nodes remain the same DOM objects
+
+  Scenario: Toggling all preserves existing todo nodes in the DOM
+    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    And a todo "Walk the dog" exists
+    And the todo nodes are saved for identity check
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then todo "Buy milk" has the completed class
+    And todo "Walk the dog" has the completed class
+    And all todo nodes remain the same DOM objects
